WEBVTT

00:32:58.670 --> 00:33:01.146
Soon, he'd be running
into a burning building.

00:33:01.170 --> 00:33:04.186
He struggled to control
how those demands affected him.

00:33:04.210 --> 00:33:07.756
CM: You can imagine, if you're always
under that kind of stress,

00:33:07.780 --> 00:33:13.700
you train your brain to be hyperaroused
or hypervigilant all the time.

00:33:13.724 --> 00:33:16.596
And that just really leads
to that anxiety.

00:33:16.620 --> 00:33:21.076
And I think that anxiety,
that's that burnout.

00:33:21.100 --> 00:33:23.112
AG: So rather than switching roles again,

00:33:23.136 --> 00:33:25.392
he decided to tackle the problem head-on.

00:33:25.848 --> 00:33:30.196
Chris is now the wellness manager
at South Metro Fire Rescue in Denver,